relations.evidence:
Essential (Required) Features:

- A pattern of recurrent episodic or continuous use of other specified psychoactive substances with evidence of impaired regulation of other specified psychoactive substance use that is manifested by two or more of the following: 
 - Impaired control over other specified psychoactive substance use (i.e., onset, frequency, intensity, duration, termination, context); 
 - Increasing precedence of other specified psychoactive substance use over other aspects of life, including maintenance of health, and daily activities and responsibilities, such that other specified psychoactive substance use continues or escalates despite the occurrence of harm or negative consequences (e.g., repeated relationship disruption, occupational or scholastic consequences, negative impact on health);
 - Physiological features indicative of neuroadaptation to the substance

